1 NAME Baltasar /de Llarena y Falcón Mesa Tello y Van de Walle/
2 GIVN Baltasar
2 _MARNM de Llarena y Falcón Mesa Tello y Van de Walle
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1747
2 ADDR
3 CITY Las Palmas
3 STAE Las Palmas
3 CTRY Spain
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 OCT 1813
2 ADDR
3 CITY Las Palmas de Gran Canaria
3 STAE CN
3 CTRY España
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baltasar was captain of the provincial militias of Gran Canaria and an officer of the Tribunal of the Holy Office of the Inquisition in Spain. As a lieutenant of the Alguacil Mayor, he was part of the executive arm
2 CONC  of the courts in charge of law enforcement (capturing and detaining defendants). He served this office until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT By a letter issued on December 16 1776 he was appointed by the Tribunal of the Holy Office as accountant (contador) of the Royal Fiscal Office of the Inquisition (Real Fisco), managing the confiscated property and goods of those c
2 CONC onvicted by the Tribunals. The position had been vacated when his father in law was named Chief Justice (Alguacil Mayor) of the inquisition tribunal of the island. This position was in turn vacated by Baltasar's grandfather, Coron
2 CONC el Baltasar Felix de Llarena.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: *Peraza de Ayala, Jose, “Historia de la Casa de Llarena (continuación) : rama segunda Casa de LLarena en Gran Canaria” originally published in Revista de historia, Vol. 4, issue 08 (1931) pp 85-89, available at Memoria Dig
2 CONC ital de Canarias <http://mdc.ulpgc.es/cdm/ref/collection/revhistoria/id/290>, (accessed Feb 17, 2013).
